 "producing_commit": "f579cc02e99b945378d050f37c392ffcc9f216d0",
 "reading": "The differences grow smoothly and decelerate, so they are accumulated integration differences rather than a per-step noise floor. Stations whose recorded clock disagrees with their file name are dropped: a march stopped by the cpu budget writes its last station part way through a chunk, and matching on the name alone compares two runs at different instants.",
 "schema": "NSC-RN-RESOLUTION-CONVERGENCE-v1",
 "scope_note": "A numerical convergence check on two resolutions, not three. Two points bound nothing and no convergence order is claimed. Agreement is evidence against a resolution artefact at these two sizes, not evidence of physics, and it does not measure the actual universe.",
 "verdict": "trajectories_agree_between_resolutions",
 "what_this_measures": "Whether the trajectory the gain is read from depends on the grid. The gain is a ratio of two amplitudes, so if the inner mass stock agrees between two resolutions at every matched station, the gain agrees and the question of whether the saturation is a grid artefact is settled for these runs.",
 "worst_relative_difference": 1.245855232765495e-06
}
